    {
      "heading": "India and Southeast Asia add capacity",
      "narrative": "Google's US$15 billion, 1GW Visakhapatnam campus, backed by Adani and Airtel, was positioned as the anchor of an Indian AI corridor with first phase targeted for mid-2028. In Singapore, Digital Realty planned a 50MW AI facility on Jurong Island while the city-state published what it called the world's first national liquid cooling standard for tropical data centers. Indonesia's Indosat spin-off Infra Fiber Teknologi launched the AI-ready RAIA Grid platform, and industry analysis highlighted a record subsea cable construction wave reshaping Asian connectivity alongside tightening power availability.",
